## SQ-SK-01 | starter kit on first join (perfBot bot = real ServerPlayer through placeNewPlayer)
> pbot spawn skbot {H1} {H2} {H3-5} minecraft:overworld survival
waitlog \[starter-kit\] .* kit given to skbot 30
reject Error occurred while handling event 'PlayerEvents\.loggedIn'
reject \[starter-kit\] could not (read|write)
sleep 2
shell L=$(sed -n 's/^level-name=//p' server.properties); U=$(python3 -c "import hashlib,uuid;print(uuid.UUID(bytes=hashlib.md5(b'OfflinePlayer:skbot').digest(),version=3))"); cat "$L/data/starterkit/tracking.json"; echo; grep -q "$U" "$L/data/starterkit/tracking.json" && echo "skbot $U in tracking.json"
> data get entity skbot Inventory
look shell: tracking.json exists with skbot's uuid under "multiplayer"; inventory holds a kit (wooden sword + 9 bread, or copper pickaxe / axe + 8 bread) and the boots / offhand shield

## SQ-SK-02 | rejoin: no second kit; with the file deleted the marker tag still blocks a kit
> tag skbot list
expect collective\.firstJoin\.starterkit
> pbot remove skbot
sleep 3
> pbot spawn skbot {H1} {H2} {H3-5} minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
count \[starter-kit\] .* kit given to skbot \( == 0
shell L=$(sed -n 's/^level-name=//p' server.properties); rm -f "$L/data/starterkit/tracking.json"; echo removed
> pbot remove skbot
sleep 3
> pbot spawn skbot {H1} {H2} {H3-5} minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
count \[starter-kit\] .* kit given to skbot \( == 0
> pbot spawn skbot2 {H1+2} {H2} {H3-5} minecraft:overworld survival
waitlog \[starter-kit\] .* kit given to skbot2 30
sleep 2
shell L=$(sed -n 's/^level-name=//p' server.properties); cat "$L/data/starterkit/tracking.json"; echo
reject Error occurred while handling event 'PlayerEvents\.loggedIn'
look skbot gets no kit on either rejoin (tag kept in its playerdata); the new bot skbot2 gets one and the file is written again (holds skbot2; skbot only if the script re-marks tagged players, which it does not: record)

